    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_96308878b74bd8bbb22a7be4502f505a1988e848e3c115cee8a0ee84a9e116c8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Normalizing the gamma ratio creates monotone comparison functions that convert the contour remainder into an explicit incomplete-gamma certificate, but the resulting absolute majorant packages truncation-order growth into G_p(M;t). The reported coefficient growth and error audit show why this certificate can track practical low-order truncations yet become useless near least-term truncation; the authors tentatively locate the lost sharpness in crude bounds and propose retaining integrand oscillation.",
