    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c2dfaf0c6578553307dc0a2213e0c81a7201293f0a35f59b9dce5b1e92dd45d2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The general Mellin-smoothed construction contains the earlier symmetric critical-line representation through a structurally special parameter choice: setting a=s/2 and p=1 aligns gamma poles with zeta's trivial zeros, leaving a transformed Mellin remainder whose functional-equation and reciprocal-scale form produces a dual incomplete-gamma sum; convergence, analytic continuation, and the critical-line scale then recover the cited formula.",
