    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ed20d4dc67481a6a7f5de25263c99b57438449e83e91e043038c7ad11d9ea4a7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The free parameters govern coupled costs rather than a single smoother: increasing p suppresses the main-sum tail more sharply but eventually shortens and worsens the useful asymptotic correction series, while increasing K can improve attainable accuracy only by moving the main-sum cutoff outward. Practical tuning therefore balances main-sum work, correction truncation, and target accuracy.",
